  "body": "In a [Twitter conversation](https://twitter.com/zcorpan/status/1489152911183855617), @zcorpan and I discussed HTML elements that could have been, and Simon brought up `<menuitem>`, which was removed in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2730. From there, I followed the link to [crbug/87553](https://crbug.com/87553), which then led me to [https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#context-menus](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#context-menus), but the ID `#context-menus` no longer exists.\r\n\r\nIn such cases, it would be great if a note appeared that guided the reader to past snapshots ([https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/942a9d5b9c0b50bf5bca275e866bb2319ebdca0c/#context-menus](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/942a9d5b9c0b50bf5bca275e866bb2319ebdca0c/#context-menus) in the concrete case). Ideally, the note even pointed the reader at the latest snapshot where the ID still appeared.",
